			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Land element submodules for build freshness\n\nUpdate all Land/Element submodules to their latest revisions, maintaining consistency across the editor's native backend, UI services, and build tooling.\n\nWind and Cocoon advance their generated artifact timestamps — catalog version dates and RouteManifest.ts compilation timestamp — to match today's codegen cycle. Output and Rest normalize shell script whitespace (tabs to 2-space indentation, pipe alignment, case branch formatting) to enforce script maintenance conventions. Mountain simplifies URI parsing in the ProvideCodeLenses IPC handler by adopting centralized Utilities::Params helpers. Sky and Worker advance to their latest submodule heads with no recorded functional changes in this sync.\n\nAll editor components remain build-consistent with no functional regressions.",
			"SHA": "a611a770ada3ab84a2a3d0c08144156cbd1bf7f8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T16:31:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Atomize state and enforce PascalCase across architecture\n\nSystematically restructure the Mountain backend to satisfy project-wide PascalCase naming conventions and improve modularization. Decompose monolithic state files into atomic modules (e.g., `MapLockError`, `DispatchDeltaWorkspaceFolders`) and rename all state structs to `Struct` to align with the reverse-hierarchical import pattern (`State::Struct`).\n\nEnforce PascalCase naming across Tauri commands, helper functions, and DTOs, including Air client components (`AirClient` → `Struct`), binary build utilities, and all `Vine`/`IPC` layer handlers. Split large service files into single-purpose modules (e.g., `Binary::Initialize`, `ExtensionManagement::Scanner`) to reduce boilerplate and enforce strict naming adherence defined in `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nCallers now use fully qualified paths (e.g., `Binary::Main::Entry::Fn`), significantly improving code clarity and maintainability across the native backend.",
			"SHA": "27f4c3762942c0fe1e3669247b9640fec6447097"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T16:18:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Update Mountain submodule to enforce PascalCase across DNS, TLS, and IPC layers\n\nUpdate the Mountain element submodule from b96ba615 to 7e880716 to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention mandated in CLAUDE.md.\n\n**Mountain:** Systematically rename Tauri commands, helper functions, and struct fields in the DNS, TLS, and IPC modules. New diagnostic commands (`DnsGetForwardAllowlist`, `TlsInitialize`) and internal utilities (`GetMemoryUsage`) are updated to PascalCase. IPC handlers for `ConfigurationBridge` and `WindAdvancedSync` now export PascalCase identifiers. Update all call sites in `WindServiceHandlers`, `ProcessManagement`, and `Track::Effect` to match the new signatures.\n\n**Impact:** Eliminates naming inconsistencies across the native backend and IPC boundary, ensuring strict adherence to the effect-based architectural principles and the project's style guide.",
			"SHA": "c2b71ca3b897313e720bc981c54c9a5e871fd000"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T16:15:12Z",
			"File": [
				"⡏⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Project): Enforce PascalCase naming across native backend and UI layers\n\nSystematically rename functions, variables, parameters, and command identifiers from snake_case to PascalCase to satisfy the project-wide naming convention defined in CLAUDE.md.\n\n**Mountain:** Refactor IPC utilities, Tauri command handlers (Dns, Tls, Process, Health), and gRPC field mappings to use PascalCase. Update `effect!` macro parameter extraction and ensure error bindings follow the `Error`/`E` convention. Align generated protobuf fields with the new casing rules.\n\n**Output:** Update TypeScript polyfills and proxy layers to match renamed Tauri commands (e.g., `ProcessGetExecPath`, `CocoonExtensionHostHealth`), ensuring the frontend correctly invokes the native backend.\n\n**Wind:** Align the Vine notification stream implementation with PascalCase identifiers (`VineSubscribeNotifications`, `VineSubscriberCount`) for all Tauri interactions.\n\n**Impact:** Eliminates style inconsistencies across the Rust/TypeScript boundary, ensuring strict adherence to the effect-based architectural principles and naming standards.",
			"SHA": "dcce41748026c6aa930bc28bb415a235176bcc97"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T15:49:11Z",
